{
    "note": "A share carrying the sender's append-only log — the record of what agents did in THEIR copy. Refused in the format rather than in a client, so that every implementation refuses it: a person sending a recipe does not think to check what travels with it, and the receiver's copy is new, so its record starts empty because nothing has happened in it yet.",
    "rule": "The share schema: a share may not carry the sender's own `.daimond/` record.",
    "says": ".daimond/",
    "stage": "decode",
}
